==Design==
===Exterior===
[[Ian Callum]] designed the XE's exterior.<ref name="CarBuyer Sept 14">{{cite news |last=Campbell |first=Russell |date=8 September 2014 |title=Jaguar XE 2015: price, specs & release date Read more: Jaguar XE 2015: price, specs & release date |url=http://www.carbuyer.co.uk/news/138785/jaguar-xe-2015-price-specs-release-date |access-date=9 September 2014 |work=CarBuyer}}</ref> The construction features bonded and riveted aluminium construction, with bolt-on front and rear crash structure and key body panels to simplify repair and decrease insurance costs.<ref name="iQAL">{{cite news |last=Holloway |first=Hilton |url=http://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/new-cars/technical-secrets-new-jaguar-xe |title=Technical secrets of the new Jaguar XE |work=Autocar |date=14 March 2014 |access-date=23 April 2014 }}</ref><ref name="Telegraph Sep 2014">{{cite news |last=Robbins |first=Alex |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/motoring/car-manufacturers/jaguar/11078112/Jaguar-XE-in-detail.html |title=Jaguar XE: in detail |work=[[Daily Telegraph]] |date=8 September 2014 |access-date=9 September 2014 }}</ref> In the event of a collision with a pedestrian, the [[active bonnet]] pops up to provide additional protection.<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" /><ref name="AutoExpress Sep Interview">{{cite news |last=Cropley |first=Steve |url=http://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/paris-motor-show/jaguar-xe-revealed-interviews-ian-callum-and-alan-volkaerts |title=Jaguar XE revealed - interviews with Ian Callum and Alan Volkaerts |work=[[Autocar (magazine)|Autocar]] |date=8 September 2014 |access-date=9 September 2014 }}</ref>

The exterior design has a [[drag co-efficient]] of 0.26.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2017 Jaguar XE 35T R-Sport 4DR RWD — 335 HP, 0-60 in 5s |url=https://www.motormatchup.com/catalog/Jaguar/XE/2017/35T-R_Sport-4DR-RWD |access-date=2026-06-09 |website=Motor Matchup |language=en}}</ref>

In 2019, the XE was facelifted, bringing updates to the exterior as well as the interior.

===Interior===
[[File:World Premiere of Jaguar XE (15158936256).jpg|thumb|XE S pre-facelift interior]]
The interior features a flush rotary gear selector which rises and becomes functional once the engine is started. The central console features an {{convert|8|in|cm|adj=on}} or optional 10.2-inch [[touch screen]], providing access to [[in car entertainment]], [[automotive navigation system|satellite navigation]] and vehicle settings. The XE features smartphone connectivity and some models allow the owner to pre-heat the interior or unlock the car remotely, using a smartphone application.<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" /><ref name="CarBuyer Sept 14" /> A laser colour [[automotive head-up display|head-up display]] is an available option.

Interior revisions in 2017<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.indiaonline.me/Technology/Automobile/Difference-between-Jaguar-XE-2016-2017-and-2018.asp|title=Difference between Jaguar XE 2016, 2017 and 2018|work=IndiaOnline|access-date=2018-02-10}}</ref> include cupholder covers, revised and higher resolution display and standard [[In-car entertainment|infotainment]] interface marketed as ''InControl Touch Pro'' reliant on a user-provided data connection [[SIM card]].

In 2019, the interior was revised with new door panels, centre tunnel and a revised [[In-car entertainment|infotainment]] system marketed as ''InControl Touch Pro Duo'', shared with other Jaguar Land Rover products. The automatic's rising rotary knob gear selector was replaced with a more conventional type marketed as the ''Sport Shift Selector''.<ref name="C&D 2020" />

==Construction==
===Platform===
[[File:Jaguar XE - 12926287943.jpg|thumb|left|Jaguar XE structure]]
The XE is the first built on the [[Jaguar Land Rover car platforms#D7a|Jaguar Land Rover iQ[Al] (D7a)]] modular platform, also used for the second generation [[Jaguar XF (X260)]] model, the [[Jaguar F-Pace]] sports utility vehicle and the [[Range Rover Velar]].<ref name="Car Oct 2014">{{cite journal|last1=Pulman|first1=Ben|title=Jaguar XE: the juice|journal=Car|date=October 2014|issue=627|pages=96&ndash;103}}</ref> The design features [[double wishbone suspension]] at the front, with similarities to the system fitted to the XF and F-Type models, the rear features an entirely new subframe mounted [[multi-link suspension]] system, marketed as ''Integral Link''. The system is costlier to manufacture but allows for greater tuning.<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" />

The major suspension components are manufactured from aluminium to reduce the [[unsprung mass|unsprung]] as well as overall vehicle mass and increase the suspension system stiffness.<ref name="CarBuyer Sept 14" /> The suspension system features sacrificial slip-fixings to protect expensive major components from damage.<ref name="Telegraph Sep 2014" /> To create the 50:50 weight balance the battery is located in the boot, consuming space normally accommodating the spare wheel. The rear boot floor and boot lid are steel, contributing to balanced weight distribution.<ref name="Carwitter.com">{{cite news |url=http://carwitter.com/2015/05/30/jaguar-xe-review-first-uk-drive-exclusive/ |title=Jaguar XE Review - First UK Drive Exclusive |work=Carwitter.com |access-date=2015-05-31 }}</ref>

Single-piston [[brake caliper]]s are provided with one of three different sizes of [[Disc brake|brake discs]] fitted, depending on the vehicle's configuration.<ref name="Autocar08Sep2014" /> An electric [[power steering]] system is fitted and the XE comes with a choice of four different road wheel sizes.<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" /> Initially there were eight available alloy wheel designs.<ref name="Autocar08Sep2014" />

===Transmission===
[[File:Jaguar XE - 12926388583.jpg|thumb|Jaguar Land Rover Ingenium engine]]
Initially offered with [[rear-wheel drive]], the [[Jaguar Land Rover car platforms#D7a|D7a]] modular architecture was designed to accommodate all-wheel drive (AWD), which was offered in November 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.jaguar.co.uk/news/jaguar-xe-awd.html |title=JAGUAR XE gains AWD and apple watch |publisher=Jaguar.co.uk |access-date=2017-02-19}}</ref>

All XE models are equipped with a [[ZF 8HP transmission|ZF 8HP45 or ZF 8HP70 eight-speed]] [[automatic transmission]],<ref name="xeforums.co.uk">Jaguar XE Technical Data: [http://www.xeforums.co.uk/viewtopic.php?f=11&t=104 ZF 8HP45], accessdate: 22. February 2017</ref> a lighter variant of the gearbox currently fitted to other Jaguar models and period competitor [[BMW 3 Series (F30)]].<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" /> A six-speed ZF manual gearbox is available on diesel models.<ref name="Autocar08Sep2014" /><ref name="CarBuyer Sept 14" />

The XE uses a traction control system marketed as ''All Surface Progress Control'', developed from the ''Terrain Response'' system fitted to Land Rover's off-road vehicles and allowing better traction in snow and ice.<ref name="Autocar08Sep2014" /><ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" /><ref name="CarBuyer Sept 14" />

==Security and safety==
Jaguar expected the XE to obtain a five star [[Euro NCAP]] safety rating which was proven in 2015.<ref>{{cite web|author=Jaguar XE |url=http://www.euroncap.com/en/results/jaguar/xe/22028 |title=Official Jaguar XE 2015 safety rating |publisher=Euroncap.com |access-date=2017-02-19}}</ref> The design features several safety features now mandatory to be considered for a five star rating, including the [[Advanced Emergency Braking System]] ([[pre-crash system]]).<ref name="WhatCar Sep 2014" />

